It shows because two separate checks are stacked, and only one of them is about switching.

The chat page shows the control whenever `listForCurrentUser` returns more than one project. You have several project records, so it renders.

Then `ProjectSwitcher` decides *how* to render from `useMultiProject()`:

```14:18:apps/frontend/src/hooks/use-multi-project.ts
	if (features.data?.['multi-project'] !== true) {
		return 'upgrade';
	}

	return isCloud ? 'switch' : 'static';
```

Self-hosted always becomes `'static'`, even with a full licence. In that mode the component just prints the current name — no dropdown. Switching is also blocked on the server (`isCloud && multi-project` licence).

So: multiple rows in the DB → name appears; self-hosted → no chevron. I’ll hide it on chat unless switching is actually allowed (cloud + licence + more than one project).
